flowchart TD
  accTitle: MOKS component architecture
  accDescr: The API, or an alert, queues an investigation in PostgreSQL. The worker claims it and runs a LangGraph StateGraph whose nodes call Investigator methods. Model calls pass through MoksChatModel and budget.complete to a provider. Tool calls reach the ToolExecutor, which calls connectors and kb_search and stores evidence and audit records in PostgreSQL. Write access exists only in the separate moks-executor process, which runs approved action plans and which the graph cannot reach.

  API["moks-api (FastAPI)<br/>RBAC, scope, rate limit, SSE"] -->|"queued row"| PG[("PostgreSQL: investigations, events,<br/>evidence, audit, budgets, knowledge")]
  PG -->|"claim: SKIP LOCKED"| I

  subgraph W["moks-worker"]
    G["LangGraph StateGraph<br/>orchestrator/graph.py"] <-->|"nodes call methods"| I["Investigator<br/>orchestrator/engine.py"]
    I --> M["MoksChatModel<br/>langchain-core chat model"]
    I --> T["StructuredTool wrappers<br/>langchain-core, planner only"]
    I -->|"baseline, logs,<br/>skills, rules"| X
    T --> X["ToolExecutor: allowlist, schema,<br/>RBAC, scope, timeout, redaction, audit"]
    M --> B["budget.complete<br/>reserve, call, settle"]
  end

  B --> L["LLM provider<br/>(six adapters)"]
  X --> C["Connectors: Kubernetes,<br/>Prometheus, Loki, Grafana,<br/>CloudWatch, Git, FinOps"]
  X -->|"kb_search"| R["RAG service<br/>rag/service.py"]
  X ~~~ EX["moks-executor (separate process)<br/>only write credentials, approved<br/>action plans, not reachable from the graph"]

